content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-104 standby unit, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, filtered-water line. The serial is unreadable because the plate is painted over.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Shaft seal is leaking steadily. The manual's troubleshooting table lists shaft-seal leakage as a fault whose corrective action is to replace the mechanical seal (5.2) and check alignment (5.4). This is a defect needing repair, not a monitored reading with a numeric limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration of 3.0 mm/s falls in Zone B (2.8 to 4.5 mm/s RMS, 'Long-term operation') of HF-300 Figure 3. It is below the 4.5 mm/s Zone C 'Restricted - plan maintenance' boundary and well below the 7.1 mm/s Zone D 'stop the pump' boundary. The limit applies to the highest reading from the two bearing housings. The report does not say whether 3.0 mm/s is RMS, which housing it was taken on, or whether it is the higher of the two.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Housing temperature of 69 C is within the manual's 'Normal up to 70 C' band, but only 1 C below the top of that band. It is below the 80 C alarm and the 90 C trip. Temperatures are measured on the housing surface.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked seal faces. This is the first-listed cause for shaft-seal leakage.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Early seal failure from the revised sleeve tolerance. This applies only if the pump is serial HF3-22000 or above and still has a component seal HF3-450 fitted. The bulletin reports early failures of HF3-450 on these builds. Applicability cannot be confirmed while the serial is unknown.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal has run dry. The seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge and the pump must never run dry. As a standby unit it may have been started or run without adequate flush.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. This is listed as a cause of seal leakage, vibration and high bearing temperature. Vibration in Zone B and a housing temperature near the 70 C normal limit are consistent with it, but they do not prove it.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before ordering or fitting a seal, establish the pump serial from asset or purchase records or other identification. Only the serial decides whether Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 applies (serial HF3-22000 and above). Do not fit any seal until the serial is confirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Take vibration readings on both bearing housings and classify the highest one using Figure 3. Record the existing housing temperature to give a baseline.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump. Keep the duty pump in service.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly using lifting equipment, because it weighs 68 kg. The casing and pipework stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller. Withdraw the seal and sleeve.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the shaft sleeve for scoring. If the serial is HF3-22000 or above, replace sleeve HF3-455 when scoring is deeper than 0.1 mm. No numeric acceptance limit is given for pumps below HF3-22000 (see open questions). Record whether the removed seal is HF3-450 (component) or HF3-450B (cartridge).",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit the new seal that matches the confirmed serial. For serial HF3-22000 and above, fit cartridge seal HF3-450B; it is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed. For serial below HF3-22000, fit component seal HF3-450. In both cases fit a new casing gasket HF3-120.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and tighten fasteners. For serial HF3-22000 and above, torque the seal gland nut to 30 Nm. For serial below HF3-22000, use Table 5 of the manual; Table 5 is not in the evidence provided, so obtain it before starting. Tighten all other fasteners to Table 5.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-align the shaft, because removing the back pull-out assembly disturbs the bearing housing. Tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before any start, confirm the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge is in place and the casing is full and vented. Never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart, re-measure vibration on both bearing housings against Figure 3 and housing temperature against the 70 C normal, 80 C alarm and 90 C trip limits. If the temperature exceeds normal or vibration enters Zone C, check grease quantity and bearing condition. If the bearings are worn, replace both as a pair.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal. Fit ONLY if the serial is confirmed as HF3-22000 or above. Stage it, but do not fit it until the serial is confirmed.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450",
      "description": "Component mechanical seal. Fit ONLY if the serial is confirmed below HF3-22000. Stage it, but do not fit it until the serial is confirmed.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket. Replace whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. Contingency spare, used if scoring is found (for serial HF3-22000 and above, if scoring is deeper than 0.1 mm).",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate the pump before work: the 55 kW, 400 V motor and the suction and discharge. Drain the pump before opening it.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, so use rated lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry. Confirm the Plan 11 seal flush before any start, including test runs.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not fit seal HF3-450 on a pump of serial HF3-22000 or above.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 h with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Contingency only, if bearing wear is found: bearing replacement (pair) is 6.0 h with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual (AQ-OM-300 Rev D) and Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 conflict on the seal. The manual specifies component seal HF3-450 with gland torque from Table 5. The bulletin, issued 14 March 2026, applies to serial HF3-22000 and above: it prohibits HF3-450 and specifies cartridge seal HF3-450B with a 30 Nm gland torque (previously 25 Nm). The bulletin keeps HF3-450 and Table 5 for pumps below HF3-22000. Because P-104's serial plate is unreadable, which document governs CANNOT be decided from the evidence. Resolve it by confirming the serial: the bulletin governs if the serial is HF3-22000 or above, and the manual governs if it is below.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The manual and bulletin differ on sleeve inspection. The manual says to inspect the sleeve for scoring but gives no limit. The bulletin sets a 0.1 mm scoring-depth replacement limit only for serial HF3-22000 and above. Do not assume the 0.1 mm limit applies to older serials.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is the serial number of P-104? The plate is painted over. The serial is needed to choose HF3-450 or HF3-450B and the matching torque. Could it be found from asset register or purchase records, or could the plate be cleaned?",
    "Table 5 of the manual (fastener torques, and the gland torque for pumps below HF3-22000) is not in the evidence. The bulletin's 'was 25 Nm' implies an earlier value, but Table 5 itself must be obtained before reassembly.",
    "Is the 3.0 mm/s vibration reading in mm/s RMS, which bearing housing was it taken on, and is it the higher of the two housings as Figure 3 classification requires?",
    "Which seal type is currently fitted (HF3-450 or HF3-450B)? This bears on the cause of failure.",
    "Has the standby unit been run dry or without seal flush? Operating history is not provided.",
    "What sleeve scoring acceptance limit applies to pumps below serial HF3-22000? None is given.",
    "Site-specific lock-out/tag-out and permit requirements are not covered by the evidence.",
    "The evidence gives no lubricant or grease quantities, in case the bearings need attention."
  ]
}
